From published data to options





flowchart LR
  d1["&lt;b&gt;Children&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;census, postcodes,&lt;br/&gt;council projection"]
  d2["&lt;b&gt;Journeys&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;walk and bus,&lt;br/&gt;routed"]
  d3["&lt;b&gt;What families ask for&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;factsheets, catchment&lt;br/&gt;preference table"]
  d4["&lt;b&gt;Places and rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;admission numbers,&lt;br/&gt;council priorities"]
  m["&lt;b&gt;Demand&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;children shared by distance,&lt;br/&gt;attractiveness, catchment,&lt;br/&gt;competition&lt;br/&gt;⚙ year · map · site · appeal"]
  c{"&lt;b&gt;Full?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;⚙ places"}
  p["&lt;b&gt;Priorities&lt;/b&gt; decide&lt;br/&gt;who is admitted&lt;br/&gt;⚙ rules"]
  r["&lt;b&gt;Refused&lt;/b&gt; re-offered:&lt;br/&gt;partner school,&lt;br/&gt;then 2nd preferences"]
  f["&lt;b&gt;Intakes&lt;/b&gt; →&lt;br/&gt;journeys&lt;br/&gt;disadvantaged mix&lt;br/&gt;budgets"]
  s["&lt;b&gt;29 options&lt;br/&gt;× 3 years&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;and the&lt;br/&gt;simulator"]
  d1 & d2 & d3 --&gt; m --&gt; c
  d4 --&gt; c
  c -- yes --&gt; p --&gt; r --&gt; c
  c -- no --&gt; f --&gt; s
  classDef data fill:#f3f5f8,stroke:#9aa7b4,color:#1f3b57;
  classDef ctl fill:#fdecd9,stroke:#d95f02,stroke-width:2px,color:#3d1c00;
  classDef run fill:#eef4fb,stroke:#1f3b57,color:#102a43;
  classDef out fill:#edf6ef,stroke:#2b7a4b,color:#102a43;
  class d1,d2,d3,d4 data;
  class m,c,p ctl;
  class r run;
  class f,s out;






Orange steps are the ones the simulator lets you change (⚙). Moving any control re-runs everything from the start — about a twentieth of a second. Every step, opened up.
